"Makes the appearance socially perfect\nThis is called, the power of respect\n\nCan hide the committed atrocities\nOr the inner corrupt\nGave one a social shield\nThis is called, the power of respect\n\nOne can give or one can get\nMight decieve in both prospect\nMany times make the curtain fall\nThis is called, the power of respect\n\nOver giving could harm the giver\nCan make them lose their circumspect\nOr it could be their tactical escape\nThis is called, the power of respect\n\nMany will oppose, might not many\nThey not always require to genuflect\nBut are compelled to bow sometimes\nThis is called, the power of respect\n\nIt could be atrocious\nAnd might have an eerie reflect\nBut one cannot question many, and\nThis is called, the power of respect\n\nThere are deserving and will always be\nThose who work for humanity's faith\nMany face tragedies but many survive\nAnd this is called, the power of respect \n\nYes one can shatter the tradition\nOne must question the intention\nOne must unite against the malintention\nAnd break the chain of irrelevant veneration"